From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:38:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 195/342] dwc2: an isochronous stream is released with its pipe

A pipe being destroyed cancels its transfers from Pipe's destructor,
where Type() no longer says it is an isochronous pipe, so the stream was
never released: the C920's second stream (a new alternate setting, a new
pipe) found no free high speed stream. CancelQueuedTransfers() now looks
for a stream of the pipe whatever its type says. The debug output of the
high speed tests is gone (serial output keeps interrupts off for
milliseconds, longer than a microframe).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp         | 18 +++++++-----------
 .../kernel/busses/usb/dwc2_isochronous.cpp     |  9 ---------
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
index 806a8b8bfe..c5ea567abb 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
@@ -686,10 +686,13 @@ DWC2::SubmitTransfer(Transfer* transfer)
 status_t
 DWC2::CancelQueuedTransfers(Pipe* pipe, bool force)
 {
-	if ((pipe->Type() & USB_OBJECT_ISO_PIPE) != 0) {
-		_CancelIsochronous(pipe, force);
+	// an isochronous stream is found by the pipe itself: a pipe being
+	// destroyed comes here from Pipe's destructor, where Type() no longer
+	// says it is an isochronous one (and its stream was never released, so
+	// the next alternate setting's pipe found no free one)
+	_CancelIsochronous(pipe, force);
+	if ((pipe->Type() & USB_OBJECT_ISO_PIPE) != 0)
 		return B_OK;
-	}
 
 	dwc2_transfer_list canceled;
 	dwc2_transfer* running[kLaneCount];
@@ -1160,15 +1163,8 @@ DWC2::_Transaction(dwc2_lane* lane, Pipe* pipe, uint32 pid, bool in,
 
 	*_nextPid = (transferSize >> HCTSIZ_PID_SHIFT) & 3;
 	result = dwc2_channel_error(status);
-	if (result != B_OK) {
-		// DEBUG M45
-		dprintf("dwc2: DEBUG device %d endpoint %d %s pid %u size %u: HCINT "
-			"%#" B_PRIx32 ", HCTSIZ %#" B_PRIx32 ", HCCHAR %#" B_PRIx32 "\n",
-			pipe->DeviceAddress(), pipe->EndpointAddress() & 0xf,
-			in ? "in" : "out", pid, size, status, transferSize,
-			_ChannelCharacteristics(pipe, in, false));
+	if (result != B_OK)
 		return result;
-	}
 	if ((status & HCINT_XFERCOMPL) == 0) {
 		if ((status & HCINT_NAK) != 0) {
 			*_nak = true;
